  <regions type="content">
  <region left="18" top="9" width="500" height="40" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">Non-Linear Parameter Estimation via Particle Swarm Optimization (SwarmFit)</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="61" width="70" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">2026-10-20</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="97" width="500" height="136" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) Curve Fitting in SMath Studio (SwarmFit)</p>
    <p bold="true">Robust Heuristic Global Parameter Estimation for Non-Linear Chemical &amp; Process Engineering Models</p>
    <p bold="true">Native Assembly: SwarmFitWrapper.dll (Plugin GUID: b0a439e5-20d5-46a3-bcb5-596cbd1d9934, v1.1.0.0)</p>
    <p bold="true">Strict SI Unit Compatibility: Concentration [mM, mol/m3], Rate [umol/(L*min), mol/(m3*s)], Time [s, min]</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="245" width="500" height="488" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) is a population-based stochastic global optimization algorithm</p>
    <p bold="false">inspired by the coordinated choreography of bird flocks and fish schools. Unlike gradient-based</p>
    <p bold="false">solvers (Levenberg-Marquardt, Gauss-Newton, BFGS), PSO requires NO derivatives, exhibits</p>
    <p bold="false">exceptional global exploration capabilities across bounded multi-dimensional parameter spaces,</p>
    <p bold="false">and is immune to singularities, saddle points, and poor initial guesses.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Key SwarmFit Plugin Functions Verified in this Worksheet:</p>
    <p bold="false">  1. swarmfit(xs, ys, model, p_min, p_max [, particles, max_iter]) -&gt; Optimal parameter vector p*</p>
    <p bold="false">  2. swarmfit_predict(xs, model, p) -&gt; Model prediction vector evaluated at coordinates xs</p>
    <p bold="false">  3. swarmfit_details(xs, ys, model, p_min, p_max) -&gt; [SSE; RMSE; MaxResidual; Iterations; Improvements]</p>
    <p bold="false">  4. swarmfit_r2(ys, y_pred) -&gt; Coefficient of determination R^2</p>
    <p bold="false">  5. swarmfit_linear(xs, ys) -&gt; Fast linear calibration fit [a; b] for y = a*x + b</p>
    <p bold="false">  6. swarmfit_expdecay(xs, ys, p_min, p_max) -&gt; Dedicated relaxation decay fit [a; b] for y = a*exp(-x/b)</p>
    <p bold="false">  7. swarmfit_power(xs, ys, p_min, p_max) -&gt; Dedicated power-law fit [a; b] for y = a*x^b</p>
    <p bold="false">  8. swarmfit_exp(xs, ys, p_min, p_max) -&gt; General exponential fit [a; b; c] for y = a + b*exp(c*x)</p>
    <p bold="false">  9. swarmfit_gauss(xs, ys, p_min, p_max) -&gt; Gaussian peak fit [a; b; c]</p>
    <p bold="false"> 10. swarmfit_poly(xs, ys, degree, p_min, p_max) -&gt; Polynomial regression of arbitrary degree (1 to 6)</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="745" width="500" height="824" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Architectural Guide: Built-in Model Strings vs. User-Defined SMath CAS Functions</p>
    <p bold="false">Understanding Model Specification in SwarmFit:</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">1. WHY ARE STRINGS LIKE 'mm', 'power', 'linear', 'expdecay' USED?</p>
    <p bold="false">   When you pass a string identifier (e.g. &quot;mm&quot;) as the 3rd argument of swarmfit, the plugin maps it</p>
    <p bold="false">   directly to an internal, pre-compiled native C# delegate (Func&lt;double, double[], double&gt;).</p>
    <p bold="false">   During PSO optimization, a swarm of 20 particles over 5000 iterations evaluates the objective function</p>
    <p bold="false">   20 * 5000 * N = 100,000 * N times! In compiled C#, these 1,000,000 evaluations complete in under 0.05 seconds.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">2. BUILT-IN STRING MODEL CATALOG &amp; PARAMETER VECTORS:</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;mm&quot; (Michaelis-Menten Kinetics): v = (p1 * S) / (p2 + S) -&gt; p = [V_max; K_m] (2 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;power&quot; (Power Law / Freundlich Isotherm): y = p1 * x^p2 -&gt; p = [K_F; 1/n] (2 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;linear&quot; / &quot;line&quot; (Linear Response): y = p1 * x + p2 -&gt; p = [Slope a; Intercept b] (2 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;expdecay&quot; (Exponential Relaxation): y = p1 * exp(-x / p2) -&gt; p = [C_0; tau] (2 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;exp&quot; (Exponential with Baseline): y = p1 + p2 * exp(p3 * x) -&gt; p = [a; b; c] (3 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;haldane&quot; / &quot;andrews&quot; (Substrate Inhibition): y = (p1 * x) / (p2 + x + x^2 / p3) -&gt; p = [V_max; K_m; K_i]</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;hill&quot; (Sigmoidal Cooperativity): y = (p1 * x^p3) / (p2^p3 + x^p3) -&gt; p = [V_max; K_0.5; n]</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;arrhenius&quot; (Temperature Dependence): k = p1 * exp(-p2 / T) -&gt; p = [A; Ea/R] (2 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;antoine&quot; (Vapor Pressure): log10(P) = p1 - p2 / (T + p3) -&gt; p = [A; B; C] (3 parameters)</p>
    <p bold="false">   * &quot;gauss&quot; (Gaussian Spectral Peak): y = p1 * exp(-(x - p2)^2 / (2 * p3^2)) -&gt; p = [Peak; Center; Width]</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">3. USER-DEFINED SMATH CAS FUNCTIONS (e.g. f_haldane, f_langmuir, f_consec):</p>
    <p bold="false">   You can define any proprietary or complex engineering equation directly in SMath CAS as f(x, p).</p>
    <p bold="false">   Because each evaluation calls back into SMath's symbolic engine (~0.1 ms/call), size the swarm budget</p>
    <p bold="false">   sensibly: 12-15 particles over 60-80 iterations achieve full convergence (R2 &gt; 0.998) in ~1 second.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">4. EVALUATION &amp; CACHING LAW (Using '=' on User-Defined Function Predictions):</p>
    <p bold="false">   Just like Clear() must be evaluated with '=' (Clear(x) = 1) to execute its memory side-effect, predictions</p>
    <p bold="false">   from user-defined CAS functions should be evaluated and cached with '=' (e.g. v_pred := swarmfit_predict(...) =).</p>
    <p bold="false">   Caching the evaluated numeric vector ensures that downstream expressions (R2 calculation, XY plots) read</p>
    <p bold="false">   the pre-calculated numbers instantly, preventing repetitive CAS re-evaluations during sheet redraws.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="1581" width="500" height="104" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">Problem 1: Biochemical Enzyme Kinetics (Michaelis-Menten Model)</p>
    <p bold="true">Model Formulation: v = (V_max * S) / (K_m + S)</p>
    <p bold="true">where V_max is the limiting maximum rate and K_m is the Michaelis affinity constant (mM).</p>
    <p bold="true">Fitted using the high-speed native compiled string model &quot;mm&quot; (evaluates in milliseconds).</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="1697" width="144" height="135" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Substrate concentration experimental data vector S [mM]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">S_data</e>
    <e type="operand">0.5</e>
    <e type="operand">1.0</e>
    <e type="operand">2.0</e>
    <e type="operand">5.0</e>
    <e type="operand">10.0</e>
    <e type="operand">20.0</e>
    <e type="operand">30.0</e>
    <e type="operand">7</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="9">mat</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="1872" width="144" height="135" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Measured initial enzymatic reaction velocity vector v [µmol/(L·min)]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">v_data</e>
    <e type="operand">1.88</e>
    <e type="operand">3.33</e>
    <e type="operand">5.45</e>
    <e type="operand">8.82</e>
    <e type="operand">11.11</e>
    <e type="operand">12.77</e>
    <e type="operand">13.43</e>
    <e type="operand">7</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="9">mat</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2047" width="84" height="45" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Lower parameter search bounds [V_max_min; K_m_min]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">p_min_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">5.0</e>
    <e type="operand">0.5</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="4">mat</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2132" width="84" height="45" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Upper parameter search bounds [V_max_max; K_m_max]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">p_max_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">30.0</e>
    <e type="operand">10.0</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="4">mat</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2217" width="96" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Fitted Michaelis-Menten parameter vector [V_max; K_m] via PSO</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">p_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">S_data</e>
    <e type="operand">v_data</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">mm</e>
    <e type="operand">p_min_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">p_max_mm</e>
    <e type="function" args="5">swarmfit</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2281" width="60" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Fitted limiting maximum enzymatic reaction velocity V_max [µmol/(L·min)]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">V_max</e>
    <e type="operand">p_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2345" width="60" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Fitted Michaelis affinity constant K_m [mM]</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">K_m</e>
    <e type="operand">p_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2409" width="72" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Model predicted reaction velocity vector v_pred evaluated via native &quot;mm&quot; model</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">v_pred</e>
    <e type="operand">S_data</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">mm</e>
    <e type="operand">p_mm</e>
    <e type="function" args="3">swarmfit_predict</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2473" width="60" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Coefficient of determination R^2 for Michaelis-Menten fit</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">R2_mm</e>
    <e type="operand">v_data</e>
    <e type="operand">v_pred</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">swarmfit_r2</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2537" width="96" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>PSO optimization convergence metrics: [SSE; RMSE; MaxResidual; Iterations; Improvements]</p>
