  <region left="18" top="6428" width="500" height="216" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">Problem 4: Substrate Inhibition Kinetics (Andrews/Haldane Bioreactor Model)</p>
    <p bold="true">Model Formulation: v = (V_max * S) / (K_m + S + S^2 / K_i)</p>
    <p bold="true">User defines custom SMath CAS function f_haldane(x, p) directly in the worksheet.</p>
    <p bold="true">Velocity exhibits non-monotonic behavior: reaches a distinct peak at S_opt = sqrt(K_m * K_i)</p>
    <p bold="true">and decreases at higher substrate levels due to biochemical toxicity / substrate inhibition.</p>
    <p bold="true">EVALUATION &amp; CACHING: Model predictions v_pred_inh are evaluated with '=' to cache results</p>
    <p bold="true">in memory and eliminate repetitive symbolic CAS recalculation across sheet repaints.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="6656" width="276" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>User-defined Haldane substrate inhibition rate function v = f(x, [V_max; K_m; K_i])</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">x</e>
    <e type="operand">p</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">f_haldane</e>
    <e type="operand">p</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">x</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
    <e type="operand">p</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">x</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
    <e type="operand">x</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
    <e type="operand">p</e>
    <e type="operand">3</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">+</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
